  "tiebreak": "If two teams are level: the higher Solve score wins, then the higher Discover score. If still level, the panel decides.",
  "final_rule": "In the Final, each team pitches its original scenario. Every assigned panel judge submits their own sheet. The Desk confirms all expected receipts, resolves remaining ties and publishes the reviewed results.",
  "bells": [
    {
      "at": "10 minutes",
      "what": "One bell: stop pitching, feedback starts."
    },
    {
      "at": "13 minutes",
      "what": "One bell: feedback is over, write your tick count."
    },
    {
      "at": "15 minutes",
      "what": "Two bells: change over. The next team sits down."
    }
  ],
  "judge_rules": [
    "Play the customer on your card, friendly and realistic. Reveal a detail only when the team asks the matching question. Anything not on your card, answer sensibly; the decision is always made in the UAE (Q21).",
    "Raise your two objections once the team starts positioning solution device. Don't add others.",
    "Tick what you hear, not what you think they meant. A tick with two parts needs both parts, or no tick. No half points. The line under each tick says what counts. All team members should speak: if one stays silent, say so in the feedback.",
    "Start the feedback by asking: 'Which type, and why?' Then give one thing that worked and one to add.",
    "Write three numbers only: the ticks (out of 10), the AI bonus tick (0 or 1), and the bonus on the badge sticker. The scorer does the arithmetic: ticks × 10, plus the AI tick × 2, plus the badge bonus."
  ],
